  [1mApproach.[0m [38;5;153mlogin()[39m keeps its [38;5;153m(username, password)[39m signature. Its return value gains a [38;5;153muserId[39m, and the submit handler
  logs it so you can see who logged in. The stub has no server to ask, so it synthesizes an ID from the username with a
  comment marking that the real value comes from the API response — same honesty as the existing [38;5;153m// Stub: would POST to
[39m  [38;5;153mAPI_ENDPOINT[39m line.

  [1mConcretely, in [38;5;153mapp.js[39m (the only file touched):[0m

  - [38;5;153mlogin()[39m — its internal [38;5;153mconsole.log("Logging in:", username)[39m becomes a post-authentication log that includes the
    [38;5;153muserId[39m, and the returned object becomes [38;5;153m{ success: true, userId, user: username }[39m. [38;5;153muser[39m stays so nothing reading it
    breaks.
  - The stub's ID: [38;5;153mconst userId = \[39muser-${username}`[38;5;153mwith a comment that the real app reads this from the[39mAPI_ENDPOINT`
    response. It's a placeholder, and labeled as one.
  - The submit handler at line 23-24 — [38;5;153mconsole.log("Login result:", result)[39m already prints the whole object, so the
    [38;5;153muserId[39m shows up there for free. I'd add an explicit [38;5;153mconsole.log("Logged in user:", result.userId)[39m only if you want a
    dedicated tracking line; otherwise I'll leave the handler untouched.

  [1mNot touched:[0m [38;5;153mindex.html[39m, [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m, [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m. No new files.

  [1mTesting.[0m There's no test infrastructure here — no [38;5;153mtest[39m script in [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m, no runner, no test files, and [38;5;153mapp.js[39m
  reaches for [38;5;153mdocument[39m at load so it isn't importable as-is. I'm not going to stand up a test harness as a side effect
  of this change. Verification is loading [38;5;153mindex.html[39m in a browser, submitting the form, and confirming the console shows
  the userId. If you'd rather I set up a real test setup (extracting [38;5;153mlogin[39m/[38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m into a requireable module and
